    "body": "fix on sn3ro:issue/2440-slot-floor-holes · PR #4320 · pinned by a_slot_with_a_hole_tangent_to_its_wall_is_still_a_slot, a_slot_with_holes_through_its_floor_is_still_a_slot and a_boss_standing_in_the_channel_is_not_a_slot (mcp_pockets) · merges when reviewed\n\nCause: the holes of p01-flange are tangent to the slot wall (x 39..45, wall at x 45). The floor's hole rings and its outer ring share one vertex, and the feature walk marks each such ring as open. So the floor had no outer ring and no feature was read. With the holes off the wall, any inner ring refused the slot. The PR fixes the two causes. On a rebuilt p01-flange, `detect_pockets` lists one open-ended slot, width 10, floor z 7, and `create` makes a Slot that posts. The heavy lanes are not run yet.\n",
